            "issue": "The associative interpretation of αὐτοῖς is contextually defensible, but the note supplies only another formulation of that interpretation. It does not disclose the materially different attachment of αὐτοῖς to τὸ ὅμοιον: humans sought to do the same as those beings did. That construction identifies the model being imitated without explicitly describing the humans as associated with those beings. Calling association the most natural reading without discussing this alternative understates the uncertainty.",
